WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-IN

00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:03.626
Friends, in this video we will have a
complete discussion about home insurance.

00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:08.737
We will see what home insurance
actually is and how we can buy it.

00:00:09.038 --> 00:00:10.538
The first thing is that

00:00:10.562 --> 00:00:14.625
home insurance is one of the most
important types of insurance for you,

00:00:14.649 --> 00:00:19.038
yet it is also one that
most people tend to ignore.

00:00:19.315 --> 00:00:20.840
Let me explain it in simple language.

00:00:20.951 --> 00:00:22.641
Whether you want to take
it or not is a different matter,

00:00:22.665 --> 00:00:26.926
but at least for your knowledge you
should know what home insurance is

00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:28.076
and what its importance is.

00:00:28.552 --> 00:00:30.599
The simple meaning of
home insurance is this:

00:00:30.623 --> 00:00:33.067
suppose you have bought a ready-made house,

00:00:33.091 --> 00:00:39.903
or you have purchased a plot and constructed
a house on it, or you have bought a flat.

00:00:39.927 --> 00:00:41.927
In any way, suppose you own a house.

00:00:42.133 --> 00:00:47.371
Now, if tomorrow there is a theft in that
house, or God forbid a fire breaks out,

00:00:47.514 --> 00:00:51.761
or there is heavy rainfall leading
to flooding around your house,

00:00:51.785 --> 00:00:56.658
and sometimes the water level
rises so much that it enters your home,

00:00:56.682 --> 00:01:01.444
reaches your rooms, damages your furniture,
and you have to face heavy losses.

00:01:01.579 --> 00:01:07.015
In other words, if any kind of
loss happens to your house—

00:01:07.181 --> 00:01:11.784
whether there is theft, an earthquake
occurs, your house collapses,

00:01:11.808 --> 00:01:17.810
or there is severe flooding, water
enters your home, walls break,

00:01:17.834 --> 00:01:21.842
valuables are stolen, furniture
gets damaged, your TV is stolen,

00:01:21.866 --> 00:01:25.040
or any loss happens to your property—

00:01:25.064 --> 00:01:29.437
then your insurance company will
compensate you and pay the claim.

00:01:29.976 --> 00:01:32.294
Why does home insurance
become very important?

00:01:33.016 --> 00:01:39.526
When we build our dream house,
the cost of building it is very high,

00:01:39.644 --> 00:01:42.557
but we tend to ignore protecting that cost.

00:01:42.922 --> 00:01:47.423
Home insurance is something you can call
one of the cheapest forms of insurance.

00:01:47.494 --> 00:01:51.787
For example, if I take a home
insurance policy worth ₹1.5 to ₹2 crore,

00:01:52.001 --> 00:01:59.463
then just as an estimate, I may get
this insurance for around ₹200 per month.

00:01:59.938 --> 00:02:01.731
There are two types of home insurance.

00:02:02.231 --> 00:02:07.001
The first is structure insurance,
and the second is content insurance.

00:02:07.025 --> 00:02:08.286
Now, what is the difference between them?

00:02:08.310 --> 00:02:11.024
Let’s take a realistic example.

00:02:11.611 --> 00:02:16.883
Suppose you purchased land in any sector,
like sectors are common in North India.

00:02:17.446 --> 00:02:20.295
You purchased a plot in some sector.

00:02:20.945 --> 00:02:26.987
Let’s assume that today the
value of this plot is ₹5 crore.

00:02:27.765 --> 00:02:29.844
The value of the plot does not matter.

00:02:29.923 --> 00:02:31.407
When we take home insurance,

00:02:31.431 --> 00:02:34.248
it does not matter whether the
plot is worth ₹5 crore or ₹50 crore,

00:02:34.486 --> 00:02:35.843
because the plot itself is not insured.

00:02:35.867 --> 00:02:36.120
Why?

00:02:36.144 --> 00:02:40.612
Because if an earthquake occurs and the house
collapses, the land will not be damaged.

00:02:40.636 --> 00:02:43.310
Similarly, if there is a flood
and water enters the house,

00:02:43.420 --> 00:02:45.420
the land still does not suffer any loss.

00:02:45.523 --> 00:02:50.523
So, when you take home insurance,
the value of the plot does not matter.

00:02:50.594 --> 00:02:54.078
Many people make this mistake, so I
am explaining it to you from the beginning.

00:02:54.212 --> 00:02:58.188
I will even show you how
to purchase home insurance.

00:02:58.879 --> 00:03:00.450
Let’s assume we have a plot.

00:03:00.474 --> 00:03:02.934
We bought a land worth ₹5 crore.

00:03:03.156 --> 00:03:06.029
On this land, I started
constructing a building.

00:03:06.053 --> 00:03:09.822
Suppose I built a three-storey
house—ground, first, and second floor.

00:03:10.448 --> 00:03:14.194
Let’s assume that the total
cost of constructing this house,

00:03:14.218 --> 00:03:16.059
including sand, gravel, cement,

00:03:16.083 --> 00:03:21.766
and all other materials along
with labour costs, was ₹1 crore.

00:03:21.957 --> 00:03:26.139
This is called the structure cost.

00:03:26.361 --> 00:03:28.361
After that, I did the interior work.

00:03:28.385 --> 00:03:34.990
I installed sofas, beds, sanitary
fittings, wallpapers, and everything else.

00:03:35.014 --> 00:03:37.569
Let’s assume the interior
cost came to ₹50 lakh.

00:03:37.894 --> 00:03:41.085
Now I want to purchase home insurance.

00:03:41.228 --> 00:03:44.760
So I will not calculate the total cost
by adding the land value of ₹5 crore,

00:03:44.784 --> 00:03:48.704
the structure cost of ₹1 crore,
and the interior cost of ₹50 lakh.

00:03:48.728 --> 00:03:51.228
I will not say that my
total cost is ₹6.5 crore.

00:03:51.538 --> 00:03:56.474
Instead, the home insurance I will purchase
will be ₹1 crore for structure insurance

00:03:56.592 --> 00:04:00.315
and ₹50 lakh for content insurance.

00:04:00.863 --> 00:04:05.561
So, I will buy a total home
insurance cover of ₹1.5 crore.

00:04:05.585 --> 00:04:06.425
Now let’s move forward.

00:04:06.449 --> 00:04:08.107
I will explain with an example.

00:04:08.131 --> 00:04:11.265
Suppose you are going
to buy home insurance.

00:04:11.947 --> 00:04:16.010
When you start the process,
the first question asked is:

00:04:16.034 --> 00:04:18.867
“What is the current
market value of the home?”

00:04:18.891 --> 00:04:22.018
Here, you need to enter the current
market value of the structure only.

00:04:22.042 --> 00:04:24.970
As in our example, we
ignore the plot value.

00:04:25.192 --> 00:04:28.659
My construction cost for
building the structure was ₹1 crore,

00:04:28.684 --> 00:04:31.978
including cement, sand, gravel, and labour.

00:04:32.002 --> 00:04:34.406
So, I will enter ₹1 crore here.

00:04:34.675 --> 00:04:38.207
Next, it will ask for the value
of belongings or contents.

00:04:38.231 --> 00:04:40.628
This includes all items in your
house such as TV, fridge, sofa,

00:04:40.652 --> 00:04:44.837
and everything that
is part of the interior.

00:04:44.861 --> 00:04:49.583
I will estimate the cost of everything—this
microphone, lights, laptop, bed,

00:04:49.607 --> 00:04:52.829
air conditioner, and all
other household items.

00:04:52.853 --> 00:04:55.520
As in our example, this cost was ₹50 lakh.

00:04:55.662 --> 00:04:57.433
So, I will enter these two values.

00:04:57.457 --> 00:04:59.600
After that, I will enter the name
of my city, for example, Mohali.

00:04:59.624 --> 00:05:01.759
Then I will check the available plans.

00:05:01.894 --> 00:05:04.497
This is how we purchase
home insurance for ourselves.

00:05:05.948 --> 00:05:10.394
We just took the example where we bought
land ourselves and built a house on it,

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:13.283
or suppose we purchased a ready-made house.

00:05:13.553 --> 00:05:15.759
But many times, people live in flats.

00:05:16.449 --> 00:05:18.663
In a flat, the land has no individual cost.

00:05:18.687 --> 00:05:21.273
Suppose you purchased
a flat worth ₹1 crore.

00:05:21.764 --> 00:05:23.955
In that case, you will enter ₹1 crore here.

00:05:24.122 --> 00:05:27.931
If the belongings inside
that flat are worth ₹50 lakh,

00:05:27.956 --> 00:05:29.956
then again you will enter ₹50 lakh.

00:05:30.344 --> 00:05:33.598
One important thing to remember
is that many housing societies

00:05:33.685 --> 00:05:37.749
already take complete
insurance for the structure.

00:05:37.773 --> 00:05:41.265
For example, suppose you go to a
society that has five or six large towers.

00:05:41.780 --> 00:05:46.892
They may have already taken insurance for
the entire society, including all the flats.

00:05:47.123 --> 00:05:48.122
So, you should check this first.

00:05:48.146 --> 00:05:51.384
Sometimes, the premium is already
included in your maintenance charges.

00:05:51.566 --> 00:05:55.019
If your society has already
taken structure insurance,

00:05:55.043 --> 00:05:58.749
then you do not need to buy
structure insurance separately.

00:05:58.773 --> 00:06:01.836
In that case, you can
purchase only content insurance.

00:06:01.860 --> 00:06:05.360
This means you do not need to enter
any amount under structure insurance.

00:06:05.385 --> 00:06:06.868
You only need to enter
the value of your belongings.

00:06:06.892 --> 00:06:12.124
For example, if the items in your house
are worth ₹50 lakh, ₹60 lakh, or ₹70 lakh,

00:06:12.149 --> 00:06:15.742
then you can enter ₹70 lakh
and click on “View Plans.”

00:06:15.829 --> 00:06:19.440
If you are the head of a society
or you manage the society,

00:06:19.464 --> 00:06:21.654
then you will also see
another option that says

00:06:21.678 --> 00:06:24.336
“Need insurance for the
entire housing society.”

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:26.399
You can click on that.

00:06:26.423 --> 00:06:28.129
Let me explain a little more deeply.

00:06:28.581 --> 00:06:31.272
There are two types of
insurance, as I told you earlier.

00:06:31.296 --> 00:06:32.486
The first is structure cover.

00:06:32.510 --> 00:06:34.906
Under structure cover, the
entire structure is included.

00:06:34.930 --> 00:06:39.517
For example, if your walls crack or
any damage happens to the structure,

00:06:39.541 --> 00:06:40.675
you will receive compensation.

00:06:40.699 --> 00:06:45.293
If your roof is damaged, the floor is
affected, tiles break, wiring is damaged,

00:06:45.317 --> 00:06:48.665
or there are plumbing-related
issues, then whatever the loss is,

00:06:48.689 --> 00:06:50.427
your insurance company will compensate you.

00:06:50.966 --> 00:06:53.091
This loss can occur in many ways.

00:06:53.115 --> 00:06:56.456
It may be due to a short
circuit, fire in the house,

00:06:56.480 --> 00:06:59.003
a cylinder blast, or any other problem.

00:06:59.027 --> 00:07:05.481
It could also be because of an earthquake,
flood, theft, riots, or any other reason.

00:07:05.505 --> 00:07:07.854
If your house suffers any
loss due to such events,

00:07:07.879 --> 00:07:10.362
your insurance company will compensate you.

00:07:10.386 --> 00:07:11.933
This becomes very important,

00:07:11.957 --> 00:07:15.949
especially in areas where
heavy rainfall happens every year.

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:17.457
In such places, people
should definitely take it.

00:07:17.481 --> 00:07:21.819
A short circuit can happen in any house,
and nobody knows when it might occur.

00:07:21.844 --> 00:07:25.905
Also, this insurance is very
affordable; it is not expensive.

00:07:25.929 --> 00:07:28.103
I will show you how to purchase it.

00:07:28.127 --> 00:07:30.341
Even if I take insurance
worth ₹1.5 crore or ₹2 crore,

00:07:30.365 --> 00:07:35.277
I can get coverage of around ₹1.5 crore
for approximately ₹200–₹250 per month.

00:07:36.641 --> 00:07:40.763
Under content insurance, items such
as TV, fridge, furniture, air conditioner,

00:07:40.787 --> 00:07:42.540
and even jewellery are covered.

00:07:42.635 --> 00:07:47.936
If the jewellery in your house gets stolen,
you can also receive a claim in that case.

00:07:47.960 --> 00:07:51.555
However, you must have the
proper bills for your jewellery.

00:07:51.745 --> 00:07:55.547
Some people purchase jewellery
in cash without paying GST,

00:07:55.571 --> 00:07:56.475
and they do not have a proper bill.

00:07:56.500 --> 00:07:57.736
In such cases, it becomes
a challenge to claim.

00:07:57.760 --> 00:07:59.537
If you have valid bills,
you will get the claim.

00:07:59.561 --> 00:08:01.561
There is also a limitation
in jewellery coverage.

00:08:01.586 --> 00:08:03.203
Some insurance companies say that

00:08:03.227 --> 00:08:09.786
if jewellery is stolen, they will give a
maximum claim of up to ₹5 lakh only.

00:08:09.811 --> 00:08:12.123
So, it depends on which
company you are purchasing from.

00:08:12.147 --> 00:08:16.147
Jewellery is included in content
insurance, but you must keep proper bills.

00:08:16.496 --> 00:08:18.496
Now let’s look at one more thing.

00:08:19.614 --> 00:08:21.550
For example, suppose we are
going to purchase insurance.

00:08:21.574 --> 00:08:23.185
So, let’s go ahead and buy it.

00:08:23.209 --> 00:08:26.562
When we purchase insurance, the
best platform I find is Policybazaar.

00:08:26.587 --> 00:08:28.783
I will provide its link
in the description box.

00:08:29.078 --> 00:08:33.434
When you click on its link,
you will reach the official page.

00:08:33.458 --> 00:08:34.807
The interface will look
something like this.

00:08:34.831 --> 00:08:37.164
Here, I entered my
name and mobile number.

00:08:37.513 --> 00:08:39.909
I am showing everything step by step

00:08:39.934 --> 00:08:43.021
so that at least you gain
knowledge for educational purposes.

00:08:43.886 --> 00:08:49.340
Now it asks, “What do
you need insurance for?”

00:08:49.522 --> 00:08:52.950
The option is “To protect
my home and belongings.”

00:08:52.974 --> 00:08:54.109
Yes, we need it for that.

00:08:54.133 --> 00:08:56.133
Many times, banks also have requirements.

00:08:56.157 --> 00:08:57.490
For example, if someone
is taking a home loan,

00:08:58.125 --> 00:09:00.831
the bank may pressure you and say
that they will give you the home loan only

00:09:00.855 --> 00:09:02.600
if you also take home insurance.

00:09:02.789 --> 00:09:04.464
In that case, remember one thing:

00:09:04.646 --> 00:09:07.464
sometimes the bank from
which you take the home loan

00:09:07.488 --> 00:09:10.043
will insist that you buy
insurance only from them.

00:09:10.067 --> 00:09:11.297
But there is no such rule.

00:09:11.321 --> 00:09:13.083
According to the guidelines
of Reserve Bank of India,

00:09:13.107 --> 00:09:14.829
you can purchase home
insurance from anywhere.

00:09:14.853 --> 00:09:19.535
Even when you buy home insurance
from a bank, it is usually more expensive.

00:09:19.718 --> 00:09:23.795
So, if you are planning to take a home loan

00:09:23.820 --> 00:09:28.321
and the bank makes home insurance
mandatory, you can buy it from anywhere.

00:09:28.345 --> 00:09:31.083
If you purchase it from
Policybazaar, it will usually be cheaper.

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:33.289
You can then show the policy to the bank

00:09:33.313 --> 00:09:34.884
and tell them that you
already have home insurance.

00:09:35.003 --> 00:09:36.955
In that case, their
condition will be fulfilled.

00:09:37.375 --> 00:09:39.328
So, you can tick this
option if it is required.

00:09:39.353 --> 00:09:41.637
Another option is “To protect
my family from home loan burden,”

00:09:41.661 --> 00:09:42.795
which you can also select.

00:09:42.819 --> 00:09:44.215
These are just conditions they ask.

00:09:44.239 --> 00:09:45.889
Then we click on “View Prices.”

00:09:46.119 --> 00:09:48.635
Now, again the same page appears.

00:09:48.753 --> 00:09:54.101
As per our example, suppose
the plot value is ₹5 crore.

00:09:54.126 --> 00:09:59.747
On that plot, the structure cost was ₹1
crore, including labour and construction.

00:10:00.049 --> 00:10:02.144
The belongings inside the
house are worth ₹50 lakh.

00:10:02.168 --> 00:10:05.080
So, we enter ₹1 crore for
structure and ₹50 lakh for contents.

00:10:05.104 --> 00:10:09.183
Then we enter the city name
and click on “View Prices.”

00:10:09.381 --> 00:10:12.714
Now here, it will start showing
different insurance companies.

00:10:13.205 --> 00:10:20.337
For example, Bharat Griha Raksha, Bajaj,
Chola, and other insurance companies.

00:10:20.361 --> 00:10:21.575
You can compare all these plans.

00:10:21.757 --> 00:10:23.662
For example, if you
take a cover of ₹1.5 crore,

00:10:23.686 --> 00:10:26.932
you may get it for around ₹258
per month, which is very affordable.

00:10:27.106 --> 00:10:30.623
Now, if I click on “View Coverages,”
I can see what all is covered.

00:10:30.647 --> 00:10:31.964
It is giving around 25 coverages.

00:10:31.988 --> 00:10:37.442
For example, natural calamities and
disaster events—such as accidental fire,

00:10:37.466 --> 00:10:41.886
lightning, earthquakes, volcanic
eruptions, or any similar problem—

00:10:41.910 --> 00:10:42.981
are covered, and I will get a claim.

00:10:43.006 --> 00:10:44.449
There are also man-made events.

00:10:44.473 --> 00:10:48.155
For example, if there is a
missile test, a bomb blast, riots,

00:10:48.179 --> 00:10:53.330
or any kind of man-made disaster that
causes damage, I will still get a claim.

00:10:53.354 --> 00:10:55.108
After that, building and
household contents are covered.

00:10:55.132 --> 00:11:02.507
This means if any household item or content
inside the house is damaged or lost,

00:11:02.531 --> 00:11:04.531
I will get full compensation.

00:11:04.745 --> 00:11:05.706
There is also a loss of rent feature.

00:11:05.730 --> 00:11:08.150
For example, suppose you
have rented out part of your house,

00:11:08.253 --> 00:11:11.745
and due to an earthquake, short
circuit, or fire, your house gets damaged.

00:11:12.015 --> 00:11:19.668
The tenant leaves, and you
start losing rent every month.

00:11:19.692 --> 00:11:21.692
In that case,

00:11:21.717 --> 00:11:24.136
the insurance company will pay you the
rent amount that you were earning earlier.

00:11:24.160 --> 00:11:26.302
There is also rent for
alternative accommodation.

00:11:26.326 --> 00:11:33.081
Suppose your house gets damaged
due to fire, and repair work is going on.

00:11:33.105 --> 00:11:35.723
During this time, you will have
to stay in another rented house.

00:11:35.747 --> 00:11:37.747
The insurance company
will pay that rent as well.

00:11:37.771 --> 00:11:39.937
All these features are included.

00:11:39.961 --> 00:11:43.024
It also covers water-related damages.

00:11:43.048 --> 00:11:46.285
Any kind of water damage is also covered.

00:11:46.364 --> 00:11:50.086
Claim-related benefits and many
add-on features are also shown here.

00:11:50.213 --> 00:11:51.569
Let me go back.

00:11:52.203 --> 00:11:54.045
Some features need to be taken as add-ons.

00:11:54.069 --> 00:11:56.703
For example, rent for
alternative accommodation.

00:11:57.552 --> 00:12:01.171
In the first company we saw, this
rent feature was already included.

00:12:01.195 --> 00:12:06.362
This means whether you are
paying rent somewhere else

00:12:06.387 --> 00:12:10.754
or losing rent from your
tenant, both are covered.

00:12:11.047 --> 00:12:13.666
But in some companies, this
has to be taken as an add-on.

00:12:13.691 --> 00:12:17.039
You need to pay a little extra
premium, maybe ₹10–₹20 more.

00:12:17.063 --> 00:12:18.753
In some plans, it is already included.

00:12:18.777 --> 00:12:20.777
So, when you compare plans,
you should check this carefully.

00:12:20.983 --> 00:12:23.102
Similarly, terrorism cover is
an add-on in some companies,

00:12:23.126 --> 00:12:24.086
while in others it is already included.

00:12:24.110 --> 00:12:29.855
This means if any loss happens due to
terrorist activities, you will get a claim.

00:12:29.879 --> 00:12:33.402
In some plans, it is included
without extra charges,

00:12:33.426 --> 00:12:34.894
while in others you need
to pay separately for it.

00:12:34.918 --> 00:12:36.806
Even if I take all these add-ons,

00:12:36.830 --> 00:12:40.163
it will only make a difference
of about ₹20–₹30 per month.

00:12:40.187 --> 00:12:41.369
So, the increase in premium
is not very significant.

00:12:41.393 --> 00:12:43.638
Still, you should compare and
decide according to your needs.

00:12:43.828 --> 00:12:45.304
There is also a personal
accident cover for self.

00:12:45.328 --> 00:12:49.359
Suppose something happens to me
and I want accident cover for myself.

00:12:49.390 --> 00:12:51.533
Then I need to check how
much accident cover I am getting.

00:12:51.558 --> 00:12:54.136
For example, if there is a short
circuit at home and I get injured,

00:12:54.160 --> 00:12:57.842
or God forbid, if the owner of the house
suffers serious damage and is no longer alive,

00:12:57.866 --> 00:12:58.833
then the claim will be paid.

00:12:58.857 --> 00:13:00.578
Some insurance companies
may give up to ₹5 lakh,

00:13:00.602 --> 00:13:01.379
while others may offer up to ₹10 lakh.

00:13:01.403 --> 00:13:02.315
So, you should compare this.

00:13:02.339 --> 00:13:03.370
There is also a personal
accident cover for the spouse.

00:13:03.394 --> 00:13:05.687
For example, if something happens
to your wife and she is no longer alive,

00:13:05.711 --> 00:13:08.956
then the insurance company will
provide a claim—₹5 lakh, ₹10 lakh,

00:13:08.980 --> 00:13:09.940
or whatever the coverage is.

00:13:09.964 --> 00:13:11.066
In some plans, this is already included,

00:13:11.090 --> 00:13:12.343
while in others you need
to take it as an add-on.

00:13:12.367 --> 00:13:14.771
Similarly, there are
additional structure covers.

00:13:14.795 --> 00:13:22.498
For example, whether you want to cover solar
panels, water tanks, or the boundary wall.

00:13:22.522 --> 00:13:25.767
The boundary wall means, for example,
if you have built a house in a sector,

00:13:25.791 --> 00:13:27.095
the main structure of
the house is in the middle.

00:13:27.119 --> 00:13:28.356
Usually, some space is
left in the front and back.

00:13:28.380 --> 00:13:32.879
There is a front wall with
a gate and a back wall.

00:13:32.903 --> 00:13:35.794
These walls also involve extra cost.

00:13:35.819 --> 00:13:39.810
The main house structure
is already covered,

00:13:39.835 --> 00:13:43.583
but you need to decide whether
you want to cover the front

00:13:43.607 --> 00:13:45.607
and back boundary walls as well.

00:13:45.631 --> 00:13:46.885
If you want, you can add this coverage.

00:13:46.957 --> 00:13:48.202
Next is jewellery and valuables.

00:13:48.226 --> 00:13:49.836
You can see this option below.

00:13:49.860 --> 00:13:51.542
You need to decide whether
you want to cover jewellery or not.

00:13:51.566 --> 00:13:54.779
Some plans already include
this, while in others it is an add-on.

00:13:55.739 --> 00:14:00.597
After reviewing all these things, if
you feel that a particular plan is better,

00:14:00.621 --> 00:14:02.462
you just need to click on it.

00:14:02.487 --> 00:14:03.851
You need to enter your details here.

00:14:03.876 --> 00:14:06.734
I will enter the details here.

00:14:06.758 --> 00:14:12.300
After entering the details, it asks
whether you have a co-owner.

00:14:12.325 --> 00:14:15.866
A co-owner means that sometimes
the property is registered in joint names—

00:14:16.136 --> 00:14:18.794
for example, in the name of both
husband and wife or any two people.

00:14:18.818 --> 00:14:21.983
If that is the case, select “I have a
co-owner” and enter the co-owner’s name,

00:14:22.008 --> 00:14:27.350
such as your wife, father,
or whoever is the joint owner.

00:14:27.374 --> 00:14:29.262
If the property is registered
in a single person’s name,

00:14:29.286 --> 00:14:30.723
then only enter that person’s name.

00:14:31.072 --> 00:14:32.929
Then it asks for the content bifurcation,

00:14:32.953 --> 00:14:34.571
meaning the distribution of
the total value of contents.

00:14:34.595 --> 00:14:36.134
We selected ₹50 lakh.

00:14:36.364 --> 00:14:40.744
For example, electronics
may be worth ₹10 lakh,

00:14:40.886 --> 00:14:46.362
furniture ₹20 lakh, and
other items ₹20 lakh.

00:14:47.386 --> 00:14:50.362
After filling this, we click on continue.

00:14:50.386 --> 00:14:54.092
After that, it asks for the complete
address of your property, where you live.

00:14:54.116 --> 00:14:56.838
You need to enter the full address.

00:14:56.863 --> 00:15:00.815
After entering the address, it will
ask for the carpet area of your house.

00:15:00.973 --> 00:15:04.171
Carpet area means the area in
which your house is constructed

00:15:04.196 --> 00:15:05.864
and the space you actually use.

00:15:05.888 --> 00:15:11.731
For example, suppose the front of a house
is 30 feet and the bakside is 50 feet.

00:15:11.755 --> 00:15:14.707
So, 30 × 50 equals 1500 square feet.

00:15:15.096 --> 00:15:17.199
This means the total constructed
area of the house is 1500 square feet.

00:15:17.326 --> 00:15:20.904
But this is the built-up area.

00:15:20.929 --> 00:15:24.087
Carpet area means the actual
usable area inside the house.

00:15:24.444 --> 00:15:26.714
Now, the house is built
within 1500 square feet.

00:15:26.857 --> 00:15:28.007
Carpet area means

00:15:28.031 --> 00:15:33.841
the space inside the house where
you can actually walk, sit, and use.

00:15:33.960 --> 00:15:35.944
So, although the house is
built on 1500 square feet,

00:15:35.968 --> 00:15:39.364
the exact usable area is
approximately 1300 square feet.

00:15:39.388 --> 00:15:44.371
This is because walls, such as
9-inch thick walls, also take up space,

00:15:44.395 --> 00:15:45.807
and that area cannot be used.

00:15:45.831 --> 00:15:48.362
Some areas may also
include slabs or structural parts.

00:15:48.386 --> 00:15:50.361
So, if the built-up area
is 1500 square feet,

00:15:50.385 --> 00:15:52.503
we can approximately select
1300 square feet as the carpet area.

00:15:52.527 --> 00:15:55.701
If the house has more than one floor, for
example, a ground floor and a first floor,

00:15:55.851 --> 00:15:57.573
then the total carpet area
will be 2600 square feet.

00:15:57.597 --> 00:16:00.732
So here, we will enter 2600 square feet.

00:16:01.050 --> 00:16:02.073
Then it asks about the building type—

00:16:02.097 --> 00:16:05.294
whether it is a multi-storey building where
you live in flats or a stand-alone house.

00:16:05.319 --> 00:16:07.895
Since we are selecting a stand-alone
house, we choose that option.

00:16:08.038 --> 00:16:10.038
Then it asks whether the
communication address is the same.

00:16:10.062 --> 00:16:12.990
If it is the same, we simply
click on the “Continue” option.

00:16:13.014 --> 00:16:16.870
After a short loading time, we
just need to make the payment.

00:16:16.894 --> 00:16:21.123
From here, you click on “Pay Securely,”
and your home insurance will be purchased.

00:16:21.147 --> 00:16:22.273
The process is quite simple.

00:16:22.297 --> 00:16:24.622
One good thing about Policybazaar is that

00:16:24.646 --> 00:16:30.013
you can compare 8–10 different
insurance companies in one place.

00:16:30.568 --> 00:16:37.785
You can see which company is offering
the lowest premium and the best coverage,

00:16:37.809 --> 00:16:39.809
and what features are included in the plan.

00:16:40.031 --> 00:16:42.269
Then you can select the best
plan according to your needs.

00:16:42.293 --> 00:16:44.538
I hope you found this session informative.

00:16:44.562 --> 00:16:46.664
I have shared the link to
Policybazaar in the description.

00:16:46.838 --> 00:16:48.166
We will meet again in the next video.

00:16:48.190 --> 00:16:49.531
For now, this is the end of the video.

00:16:49.555 --> 00:16:51.555
Thanks for listening, and thank you all.

